xt":"speed meet on the cycle; a second pass from "},{"code":"start","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" finds the first cyclic vertex, and a third"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lap measures the cycle. O(μ + λ) time, O(1) memory, and states need only be "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/floydcycledetection(from:successor:)"},"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs/brentCycleDetection(from:successor:)":{"title":"brentCycleDetection(from:successor:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/brentcycledetection(from:successor:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/brentCycleDetection(from:successor:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The tail and cycle of the orbit of ","type":"text"},{"code":"start","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" under ","type":"text"},{"code":"successor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", by Brent’s algorithm (R. P.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Brent, “An improved Monte Carlo factorization algorithm”, BIT 20 (1980) 176–184): the tortoise","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"teleports to the hare at each power of two, which measures the cycle length directly; a second","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass with the hare λ steps ahead finds the first cyclic vertex. O(μ + λ) time, O(1) memory, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"states need only be ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"brentCycleDetection","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind